  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Discussions surrounding a potential new vice president have emerged in Indonesia, focusing on Sufmi Dasco Ahmad, who currently serves as a Deputy Speaker of the House of Representatives. Support for his candidacy has been expressed by diverse groups, including political figures and organizations like the Indonesian Tarbiyah Association (PP Perti) and figures such as the Governor of West Java. Proponents argue that his experience makes him a suitable candidate to assist President Prabowo Subianto. In response to the growing discourse, President Jokowi clarified that he has not issued any instructions regarding these developments and remains committed to supporting the current administration. Sufmi Dasco Ahmad has maintained that the selection of a vice president remains the exclusive prerogative of the head of state, while the Gerindra Party has highlighted that specific criteria are necessary for any potential successor.",
